      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T20:08:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did some measurements on my M1, 16kb and 1mb are fixed buffer sizes, \"dynamic\" is this CL:\n\n`grmtl`\n               16kb   1mb    dynamic  %-age\n    Arcs       5.2ms  4.9ms  4.8ms    7.7%\n    SuitsClip  6.2ms  5.7ms  5.7ms    8.1%\n    Suits      7.1ms  6.6ms  6.4ms    9.9%\n    Leaves     .77ms  .72ms  .76ms    1.3%\n    Paths      3.1ms  2.9ms  2.9ms    6.5%\n    \n`grdawn_mtl` improvements were comparable, although in all experiments Suits and SuitsClip were slower than `grmtl` (7-8ms vs. 5-6ms), whereas the others were much closer in absolute magnitudes. \n\nSo to me it looks like we\u0027re getting a solid 5+% improvement on the scenes that have large amounts of content and the dynamic strategy is getting very similar levels of performance compared to just being very pessimistic with buffer sizes.",
      "parentUuid": "12973ac1_c4c6f9dc",
      "revId": "38ba0538632d01eef8e6c5698b7606f4e2788200",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
